# PidgeIoT vulnerability disclosure, per RFC 9116.
#
# Two files carry this text. security.txt.unsigned is the source anyone
# edits; security.txt is what the origins serve, either a copy of that
# source or a cleartext OpenPGP signature over it. A dovecote test compares
# their payloads, so the served document cannot drift from the source.
#
# fancier serves it as a static asset, dovecote bakes it into the API
# worker with include_str!, and the status worker imports it as a text
# module, so all three origins answer with the same document. Renew Expires
# before it passes, and re-sign when you do: a security.txt past its own
# Expires is stale by its own terms.

Contact: mailto:security@pidgeiot.com
Encryption: https://pidgeiot.com/.well-known/pgp-key.txt
Expires: 2027-02-26T00:00:00Z
Preferred-Languages: en
Canonical: https://pidgeiot.com/.well-known/security.txt
Canonical: https://api.pidgeiot.com/.well-known/security.txt
Canonical: https://status.pidgeiot.com/.well-known/security.txt
Policy: https://github.com/justins-engineering/pidgeiot/blob/main/SECURITY.md
